Original commit body from 431d47d9da4546186c8551a1b6aecd979b09e000:

The previous commit asserted that ADR-0039's ruling 5 Stage B had not
landed and that "no generator exists in scripts/". Both are false, and
the claim reached four surfaces: ADR-0039's Status line, ADR-0005's
Status line and amendment, the README index row, and the changelog.

Stage B shipped. The per-evidence-type confidence table IS generated
from the registry: the projection lives in docs/concept-axes.md, is
emitted from evidence_types.EVIDENCE_TYPES by
scripts/generate-concept-axes, is held fresh by that script's --check
gate in .githooks/pre-commit, and is pinned by
tests/test_generate_concept_axes.py::test_every_seeded_pathway_appears_with_its_value.
Spec sec 12 states this explicitly and links to it — "The per-pathway
values are generated, not transcribed here."

How the error was made, since the method is the reusable part: I
searched `ls scripts/ | grep -i confidence`, found nothing, and treated
that as absence. The generator is named for what it emits
(generate-concept-axes), not for the value it carries. A second check
that could have caught it — grepping the spec for AUTO-GENERATED — was
run against a hardcoded line range that my own edits had already
shifted, so it scanned the wrong section and returned nothing too. Two
negatives, both from looking in the wrong place, taken together as
evidence.

ADR-0039 is now Accepted — Implemented (all five rulings).

ADR-0005's caveat survives but its reason was wrong. Its detector-tier
constants (0.95 / 0.99 / 0.70-0.85) really are unguarded hand-written
prose — `confidence=0.95` is a literal at a dozen entrypoints.py call
sites, 0.99 appears only in a comment, and the sec 8 tier table has no
generator. But they were never in Stage B's scope: Stage B regenerates
the EvidenceTypeSpec table, and entrypoint tiers are a different
population in no registry. The 2026-06-11 amendment predicted Stage B
would cover them; that prediction was wrong about scope. Giving those
constants a registry and a projection is new work, not the completion
of Stage B.

